# DWT routes

Single file (about 1,050 lines), edited by multiple people. Routes are grouped by version:

- `registerVersionRoutes(version)` — shared by `v1` and `v2` (a few `if (version === 'v2')` branches).
- `registerV3Routes()` and `registerV4Routes()` — one function each, called straight after its definition.
- Unversioned redirects to `v1` sit at the very end. Leave them alone.

Add routes inside the relevant version's function, under the relevant section banner (`// --- Software providers ---`, `// --- API keys ---`). Don't add them at the top or bottom of the file, and don't add routes for one version to another version's function.

Each version function follows the same shape — copy it when starting a new version:

```js
function registerV4Routes () {
  const base = '/v4'
  const view = (page) => `v4/${page}`

  router.use(base, (req, res, next) => {
    res.locals.version = 'v4'
    next()
  })

  // Data in session, with its own key per version — no backend.
  function providerList (req) {
    if (!Array.isArray(req.session.data.softwareProvidersV4)) {
      req.session.data.softwareProvidersV4 = []
    }
    return req.session.data.softwareProvidersV4
  }

  // --- Section name ---

  router.get(`${base}/page-name`, (req, res) => {
    res.render(view('section/page-name'), { /* data for the view */ })
  })
}
```

- A page's GET and POST use the **same URL** (e.g. `GET` and `POST` `/v4/software-providers/add`). Don't add `-answer` routes.
- Validate on the server. On error, re-render the same view with `errors` and `errorList` (for `govukErrorSummary`) and the submitted values. On success, redirect to the next page.
- Build every URL from `base`, never hard-code `/v4/`, so the function can be copied to the next version.
- Keep logic in `routes.js` or the shared helpers in `app/data/` (e.g. `software-providers.js`), not in the view.
- Persist data in `req.session.data` under a key that is unique to the version (e.g. `softwareProvidersV4`).
- Comments explain why, in plain English, so a non-developer can follow the file.
